<h1>Bug and security disclosure</h1>
<p>Report a security vulnerability, privacy concern, reliability defect, or product bug directly to <a href="mailto:founders@pilotprotocol.network?subject=Pilot%20Protocol%20disclosure">founders@pilotprotocol.network</a>.</p>

<h2>Include</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Your contact email and optional name or handle.</li>
  <li>Issue type and reporter-assessed severity.</li>
  <li>Affected component, URL, version, endpoint, or app identifier.</li>
  <li>A concise summary, technical detail, safe reproduction steps, and potential impact.</li>
  <li>Any prior contact or intended disclosure timeline.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Safe reporting</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Do not include live credentials, private keys, customer data, or destructive payloads.</li>
  <li>Use minimal, redacted proof and stop when continued testing could create harm or unauthorized access.</li>
  <li>Do not persist access, alter data, degrade service, or affect another party.</li>
  <li>Give the team a reasonable opportunity to investigate and remediate before publication.</li>
</ul>
<p>This reporting channel does not promise a bounty, safe-harbor determination, or fixed response time. See <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>.</p>
</PlainLayout>
